{"sequence":40,"type":"assistant_text","sourceId":"conversation:8f3cd68f-a173-4c4b-9ef9-85ef65b8f194:text:0","timestamp":"2026-09-29T17:50:10.714Z","text":"Confirmed the bug. In `expandGraphFacts`, the one-hop traversal `(entity)-[rel]-(neighbor)` also walks back across the `MENTIONS` edge to the originating `Chunk` node itself (since it's an undirected match). `describe()` has no case for label `\"Chunk\"`, so it falls into the `default -> label + \" \" + props` branch — which dumps the **entire node property map, including the 1536-float `embedding` vector**, as raw text into the graph facts. That happens for every entity a chunk mentions, so it's a guaranteed multi-thousand-token bloat per chunk, easily blowing past the 128k context limit once you factor in the system prompt and multiple retrieved chunks."}